        "role": "user",
        "content": "{\"context\":[{\"id\":\"c1\",\"text\":\"Gross margin percentage decreased driven by the continued investments in AI infrastructure as well as sales mix shift to Azure, offset in part by efficiency gains in Azure.\"},{\"id\":\"c2\",\"text\":\"Operating expenses increased $1.4 billion or 7% driven by continued investments in research and development compute capacity, AI talent, and data to support product development that benefits the entire portfolio.\"},{\"id\":\"c3\",\"text\":\"Cost of revenue included an unfavorable foreign currency impact of 2%.\"},{\"id\":\"c4\",\"text\":\"More Personal Computing\"}],\"filing\":\"MSFT 10-K\",\"section\":\"Part II Item 7\",\"sentences\":[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > More Personal Computing\",\"text\":\"Revenue decreased $597 million or 1%.\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > More Personal Computing\",\"text\":\"Windows and Devices revenue decreased $230 million or 1%.\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > More Personal Computing\",\"text\":\"Windows OEM and Devices revenue decreased slightly driven by a decline in Devices, offset in part by Windows OEM growth of 5% with inventory levels that remained elevated.\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > More Personal Computing\",\"text\":\"XBOX revenue decreased $1.7 billion or 7% driven by declines in XBOX content and services and XBOX hardware.\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > More Personal Computing\",\"text\":\"XBOX content and services revenue decreased 5% on a prior year comparable that benefited from strong first-party content performance, offset in part by growth in XBOX Game Pass.\"},{\"id\":\"s6\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > More Personal Computing\",\"text\":\"XBOX hardware revenue decreased 29% driven by lower volume of consoles sold.\"},{\"id\":\"s7\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > More Personal Computing\",\"text\":\"Search advertising revenue increased $1.3 billion or 9%.\"},{\"id\":\"s8\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > More Personal Computing\",\"text\":\"Search advertising revenue excluding traffic acquisition costs increased 12% driven by higher search volume and revenue per search, as well as benefit from third-party partnerships.\"},{\"id\":\"s9\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > More Personal Computing\",\"text\":\"Operating income increased $220 million or 2%.\"},{\"id\":\"s10\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > More Personal Computing\",\"text\":\"Cost of revenue decreased $1.8 billion or 7% driven by lower hardware sales.\"},{\"id\":\"s11\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > More Personal Computing\",\"text\":\"Gross margin increased $1.2 billion or 4% driven by growth in Search advertising and Windows OEM.\"},{\"id\":\"s12\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > More Personal Computing\",\"text\":\"Gross margin percentage increased driven by sales mix shift to higher margin businesses.\"},{\"id\":\"s13\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > More Personal Computing\",\"text\":\"Operating expenses increased $940 million or 6% driven by impairment and other related expenses in our XBOX business and continued investments in research and development compute capacity, AI talent, and data to support product development that benefits the entire portfolio.\"},{\"id\":\"s14\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > More Personal Computing\",\"text\":\"Operating income included a favorable foreign currency impact of 2%.\"},{\"id\":\"s15\",\"section_path\":\"Part II Item 7 > Research and Development\",\"text\":\"Research and development expenses include payroll, stock-based compensation expense, employee benefits, and other headcount-related expenses associated with product development.\"}]}"
